% ============================================================================
% plant-tropisms.query.adj — a worked recall over the biology plant-tropisms
% library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what does a phototropism
% respond to?": it states no botany fact of its own — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?` against
% the `tropism_stimulus` rows and returns the stimulus + the table's source/
% locator/trust. The fourth query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the stimulus
% `gravity`, recall its tropism — gravitropism). A word that is not one of these
% tropisms abstains honestly — the engine never invents a stimulus.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli plant-tropisms.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "plant-tropisms.adj"

? tropism_stimulus(phototropism, $Stimulus)   % expect light
? tropism_stimulus(thigmotropism, $Stimulus)  % expect touch
? tropism_stimulus(hydrotropism, $Stimulus)   % expect water
? tropism_stimulus($Tropism, gravity)         % reverse bind — expect gravitropism
? tropism_stimulus(sound, $Stimulus)          % expect abstain — there is no "soundtropism" row; sound is not one of these tropisms
